Yeah, that sounds like a bug in the DS port.  When the player changes
levels, Nethack saves the state of the previous floor to a file, and
loads it back into memory when the player returns to that floor.  It
performs some internal checks to ensure that these files are not
tampered with, and if they are it ends the game as a trickery.

This should probably be reported to the guy who maintains the DS port
of the game.  It probably is something wrong concerning the game's disk
analogue.

